# LifeOS does NOT load this file (ADR 0014). Nothing here takes effect by being in .env.
# Put the variables you need in ~/.zshrc as `export NAME=value`, then open a new Terminal window
# and run `corepack pnpm update-app`. See README, "Where the code and the data live".
#
# Why not load .env: a stale .env left in the code folder could silently point the app at the wrong
# data folder or device ID. Shell variables are visible, per Mac, and shared by every LifeOS command.

# Required. The data folder in Google Drive; LifeOS refuses to start unless it holds .lifeos/schema.md.
# LIFEOS_DATA_ROOT="$HOME/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-<your-email>/My Drive/Claude Working Space/Personal/LifeOS App/data"
# Backups, local to each Mac and outside Google Drive. Default: ~/LifeOS-backups
# LIFEOS_BACKUP_ROOT="$HOME/LifeOS-backups"
# A different, fixed name on each Mac, e.g. desk-mac and laptop. Default: the Mac's host name.
# LIFEOS_DEVICE_ID=desk-mac
# Minutes without activity before this Mac gives up the write lease (ADR 0015). Default: 15
# LIFEOS_IDLE_RELEASE_MINUTES=15

# Rarely needed.
# LIFEOS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# LIFEOS_PORT=4310

# Google Calendar OAuth: enter the client ID and secret on the Settings page (stored in macOS Keychain).
# These variables are only an optional development bootstrap.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=example.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=temporary-development-bootstrap-only
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:4310/api/v1/connections/google/callback
